{%- comment -%}sugar:snippets/media-sizes-scope.liquid@2.1.1{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Narrows the `sizes` hint of every Media block inside a multi-column parent.

  A Media block cannot know the column it lands in, so on its own it tells the browser it is
  half the window wide on desktop and the full window on mobile. Inside a four-up grid the
  browser then downloads a file four times wider than the cell. The parent does know its
  column count, so it captures its children and passes them through here.

  The Media block writes its hint in a form that can be divided more than once:
    (min-width: 750px) calc(50vw / 1.0000), calc(100vw * 1.0000)
  The first parent on the way up restarts the desktop figure from the full window and divides
  by its own columns; every parent after that divides again, so a three-up grid inside a
  half-width column ends up at a sixth of the window. A parent that is a single column on a
  breakpoint leaves that half of the hint alone. Gaps and page padding are ignored, so the
  figure always errs on the wide side: a slightly larger file, never a blurry one.

  Accepts:
  - html: {String} the captured children
  - d: {Number} how many of this parent's children share a row on desktop (may be fractional)
  - m: {Number} the same for mobile
  - cap: {Number} optional, the parent's fixed maximum width in px (a Container set to a custom
    width). Applied only to a hint no inner parent has narrowed yet; an outer parent still divides
    the figure inside it.
  - full: {Boolean} optional, the parent spans the section's width (a Custom Columns column). A
    hint no inner parent has narrowed restarts from the full window even when d is 1, since the
    Media block's own half-window guess is only right beside a product gallery.

  Usage:
  {%- capture _children -%}{% content_for 'blocks' %}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- render 'media-sizes-scope', html: _children, d: 3, m: 2 -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign _mss_out = html
  assign _mss_d = d | default: 1 | times: 100 | floor | divided_by: 100.0
  assign _mss_m = m | default: 1 | times: 100 | floor | divided_by: 100.0
  assign _mss_cap = cap | default: 0 | times: 1
  if _mss_cap > 0
    assign _mss_cap_d = 'min(' | append: _mss_cap | append: 'px, calc(50vw / 1.0000))'
    assign _mss_cap_m = 'min(' | append: _mss_cap | append: 'px, calc(100vw * 1.0000))'
    assign _mss_out = _mss_out | replace: 'calc(50vw / 1.0000)', _mss_cap_d | replace: 'calc(100vw * 1.0000)', _mss_cap_m
  endif
  if _mss_d > 1
    assign _mss_again = '100vw / 1.0000 / ' | append: _mss_d | append: ' /'
    assign _mss_first = '100vw / 1.0000 / ' | append: _mss_d | append: ')'
    assign _mss_out = _mss_out | replace: '100vw / 1.0000 /', _mss_again | replace: '50vw / 1.0000)', _mss_first
  elsif full
    assign _mss_out = _mss_out | replace: '50vw / 1.0000)', '100vw / 1.0000 / 1)'
  endif
  if _mss_m > 1
    assign _mss_mobile = '100vw * 1.0000 / ' | append: _mss_m
    assign _mss_out = _mss_out | replace: '100vw * 1.0000', _mss_mobile
  endif
-%}
{{- _mss_out -}}
